WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.899
(staccato string music)

00:00:00.899 --> 00:00:03.730
- [Narrator] Vietnamese food
is bountiful in Portland.

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:07.060
From Pho to Bành Mì, it's hard to miss.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.590
But among your classic
Vietnamese restaurants,

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:11.430
there is one tiny place

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.410
that makes soups from
different regions of Vietnam

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:17.423
that you can't find anywhere
else outside the country.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.320
How that place came to be involves the CIA

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.197
and is one hell of a journey.

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:30.026
(staccato string music)

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:34.777
(light chamber music)

00:00:36.427 --> 00:00:39.094
(keys rattling)

00:00:48.985 --> 00:00:51.985
(light piano music)

00:00:54.376 --> 00:00:57.126
(cameral clicks)

00:01:01.031 --> 00:01:02.820
(cameral clicks)

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.120
- [Narrator] By the
time the U.S. pulled out

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.600
of the Vietnam War in 1973,

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.240
William was put in jail
by the Communist regime.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:12.847
He would spend the next 10
years of his life in prison.

00:01:27.478 --> 00:01:28.460
(camera clicks)

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.138
- [Narrator] After being released,

00:01:30.138 --> 00:01:31.690
(camera clicks)
it took William six years

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.390
to reunite with his family
(camera clicks)

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:34.753
who settled in Portland.

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:38.470
Away from his homeland
and missing the comforts

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.723
of home cooking, he had an idea.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.450
- [Narrator] Six days a week,

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:56.890
William and his wife, Christina,

00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:00.000
come in and make two
distinct soups from scratch,

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.950
each soup representing a
different part of Vietnam.

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:06.760
That's it, a two-item
menu that changes daily.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.493
And by early afternoon, they sell out.

00:02:24.582 --> 00:02:25.857
(knife chopping methodically)

00:02:25.857 --> 00:02:28.000
- [Narrator] 5:00 a.m.
wake-up, six days a week,

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.410
complex broths from scratch,
people half their age

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:33.130
wouldn't be able to last long.

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:34.803
So how are they still going?

00:02:38.845 --> 00:02:40.454
(William laughs)

00:02:40.454 --> 00:02:43.787
(staccato string music)

00:02:47.136 --> 00:02:50.053
(octave bell tone)

